---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Excerpt from "../../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Inferred from "../../components/Inferred.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";

const REQ = "server/src/iki_server/entities/requests.py";
const STATES = "server/src/iki_server/entities/states.py";
const MODELS = "server/src/iki_server/entities/models.py";
const TEST = "server/tests/test_core_facility.py";

const H = {
  short: "When a deliverable goes back, and when a request is done",
  how: "Release, what's final after it, and coverage",
  example: "Long-read sequencing from a core facility, released and delivered",
  rules: "Release, correction and completion in full",
  ref: "Code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "release", label: "Release" },
  { id: "final", label: "What's final after it" },
  { id: "completion", label: "Completion and coverage" },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      A deliverable is the service's alone until it's set to one of its type's released states. Then
      it's linked into the asking project once, for its request, audited
      as <code>request.result_released</code>, and the request's creator and watchers are told. Released
      after a signed independent review, it's final. The service can set the request to its completed
      state only when at least one deliverable is back, every recorded deliverable is back, and every
      commissioned subject is covered by a returned deliverable: directly, through a recorded aliquot,
      or through the draw that took a sample from it (<Adr n={[132, 149, 179, 211]} />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <h3 id="release">Release</h3>
    <p>
      Every state change calls <code>released()</code>. When the field and state are the ones the
      type releases on, it finds the request sent to the deliverable's project, checks again that the
      deliverable's subject is on the request, and links the deliverable into the asking project
      with <code>via_request</code>. A deliverable already linked back for this request isn't linked or told
      again. One already in the asking project some other way is marked as released there, so it stays.
      A service that has stopped sharing its entities can't release (<Path p={REQ} sym="def released(" />, <Path p={STATES} sym="requests.released(" />). Until release, the asking project can't read the
      deliverable or its files: <PageLink to="Sharing across projects" /> says how that's held.
    </p>
    <p>
      The audit event carries the reviewed, signed and released revisions,
      and <code>GET /entities/&#123;ref&#125;/request</code> reads them back as the request's release
      receipts (<Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/requests.py" sym="class ResultReleaseOut(" />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="final">What's final after it</h3>
    <p>
      When the release signature follows a separately signed review, the signed document names the
      reviewed revision and Iki keeps it as <code>released_review_revision</code>. The database holds
      that such a deliverable stays locked, at exactly two revisions past the reviewed one, and its
      values and states can't change again (<Path p={MODELS} sym='name="iki_released_review_locked"' />, <Path p={STATES} sym="def _final_release(" />). Before release, a reasoned correction under lock
      returns each state to its <code>on_edit</code> target, and the deliverable is submitted and
      reviewed again (<Adr n="0179" />, <PageLink to="Locks and corrections" />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="completion">Completion and coverage</h3>
    <p>
      A request type's <code>completed</code> names the service state that closes it, Delivered
      in <code>iki/requests</code>. Setting it asks <code>delivery_refusal()</code>, which refuses while:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>a commissioned subject has no returned deliverable: "Tube B has no returned result yet";</li>
      <li>
        a recorded deliverable isn't returned: not in a released state, not linked back for this
        request, or, for a signed release, without signatures on its last transition;
      </li>
      <li>no deliverable has been returned at all.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The commissioned subjects are the project records in the request's <code>materials</code> fields;
      a registry entry names a molecule, not a tube, so it isn't one (<Path
        p={REQ}
        sym="def materials_of("
      />, <Path p={REQ} sym="def delivery_refusal(" />, <Path p={STATES} sym="requests.delivery_refusal(entity)" />). A
      deliverable covers the subjects its <code>material</code> reaches:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file={REQ} start="^def _covered_subjects\(" />
    <p>
      For an <code>iki/samples.Sample</code>, the ledger decides, not the sample's declared source:
      the <code>drawn</code> movement whose <code>used_in</code> is the sample names the tube or lot it
      debited. From a tube, the walk follows its <code>aliquot</code> movement back to the tube it was
      split from, through any number of splits, or a registered aliquot's declared parent. A sample
      drawn from an unrelated tube covers nothing, and several deliverables on one tube cover it once
      (<Adr n={[132, 211]} />). Drawing is on <PageLink to="Draws and samples" />.
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      The core in <Path p={TEST} sym="def _sequencing(" /> sequences tube CEY652, which the asking
      project split twice before sending. The deliverable names the second aliquot and run
      ERR13376132, and covers CEY652 through both splits. It's corrected after review, submitted and
      reviewed again, and released by QA. Then:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        The request's release receipt names the corrected review's revision, the signed revision and
        the released revision; the earlier report stays readable in the deliverable's history.
      </li>
      <li>
        The asker adds Tube B to the request. Delivered is refused with "Tube B has no returned result
        yet" until a released deliverable covers it, and an unsuccessful outcome covers it too.
      </li>
      <li>A recorded draft deliverable blocks Delivered until it's released as well.</li>
      <li>Once the request is Delivered, a new deliverable for it is refused as already delivered.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      <Path p={TEST} sym="def exercise_sample_delivery(" /> runs the same rule through samples for each
      pair: a Plain sample drawn from a sent tube, a Research sample drawn directly from a sent lot,
      and a QC sample drawn from an aliquot of an aliquot. In each, a deliverable on a sample is
      refused before its draw. In the Research case, one on a sample drawn from a core tube that holds
      the lot is refused too, since that draw debited the tube, not the lot.
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="Release, and after it" open>
        <p>
          A release is told once: a deliverable already linked back for this request isn't linked again,
          and one released, set back and released again isn't released twice. Release is refused if its
          material isn't covered by the request any more (<Path p={REQ} sym="MATERIAL_REFUSAL = (" />). The
          released states neither declare nor receive an <code>on_edit</code> return, so a
          correction can't release (<PageLink to="Request and deliverable types" hash="rules" />).
        </p>
        <p>
          <Inferred why="Read from ResultSpec.requires_review; no test asserts it.">
            A Research deliverable is released by a single review signature, so no earlier reviewed
            revision is kept and its receipt has none.
          </Inferred>
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Recording a deliverable">
        <p>
          A deliverable must be made in the project the request was sent to. Its material must be a
          subject on the request, a recorded aliquot of one, or a sample drawn from either; one for a
          request with no subjects names none. Once the request is in its completed state, no new
          deliverable is recorded for it (<Path p={REQ} sym="def check_result(" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Who is told">
        <p>
          The asking project's people its type names are told as each deliverable comes back;
          in <code>iki/requests</code>, the request's creator and watchers (<Adr n="0142" />, <Path
            p="plugins/requests/types/request.yaml"
          />). What events reveal to whom is on <PageLink to="What events disclose" />.
        </p>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={REQ} sym="def released(" />, <Path p={REQ} sym="def delivery_refusal(" />: release and completion</li>
        <li><Path p={TEST} />: the facility flows, end to end</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0142" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0149" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0179" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0211" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
